.TH AGENTX-IFSTACK 8 "September 2026" "agentx-ifstack" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
agentx-ifstack \- serve Linux interface stacks through AgentX
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agentx-ifstack
.RB [ \-\-config " PATH" ]
.RB [ \-\-socket " PATH" ]
.br
.B agentx-ifstack
.RB [ \-\-help " | " \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agentx-ifstack
serves the IF-MIB ifStackTable to an SNMP master through an AgentX Unix socket.
Enable
.B master agentx
in snmpd.conf before enabling this service.
.PP
The daemon runs
.B ip \-details \-json link show
in its network namespace to find bonds, bridges, and interface layers.
It serves GET, GETNEXT, and GETBULK requests.
Rows use the higher interface index first and the lower interface index second.
Required zero-index boundary rows are included.
Writes are rejected.
.PP
Topology refresh is demand driven.
After the cache expires, the next read request refreshes it.
A refresh failure returns an AgentX processing error.
The next read request retries the refresh.
.PP
The daemon reconnects and registers again when the master disconnects.
Retry delays start at one second and double to a maximum of 30 seconds.
A session that lasts at least 30 seconds resets the delay.
A missing master does not cause the daemon to exit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Read configuration from PATH instead of /etc/agentx-ifstack.toml.
An explicitly selected file must exist.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
Override the socket in the configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file uses TOML and accepts exactly four keys.
Omitted keys use built-in defaults.
An absent default file uses all built-in defaults.
An absent explicit file, malformed TOML, an unknown key, or an invalid value
causes a nonzero exit before any connection attempt.
.TP
.B socket = "/var/agentx/master"
AgentX master Unix socket path.
The path must not be empty.
.TP
.B refresh = 5
Seconds to cache interface topology.
The value must be an integer of at least 1.
.TP
.B priority = 127
AgentX registration priority, from 1 to 255.
Lower values win when registered regions overlap.
.TP
.B log_level = "info"
Default log filter: error, warn, info, debug, or trace.
Logs go to standard error without timestamps.
An idle healthy daemon is quiet at info.
.PP
Override order is built-in defaults, then file values, then command-line flags.
The
.B RUST_LOG
environment variable overrides the log filter.
Restart the process to apply configuration changes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/agentx-ifstack.toml
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I /var/agentx/master
Default AgentX master socket.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM and SIGINT terminate the process with their default signal actions.
There is no configuration reload signal.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates that help or version output completed.
A configuration or command-line error exits with status 1.
During normal operation the process runs until terminated.
Connection and refresh failures do not terminate it.
.SH NOTES
The service runs as root because /var/agentx is normally mode 0700 and owned by root.
An unprivileged process cannot traverse that directory.
The systemd unit removes all capabilities and permits Unix and netlink sockets.
It needs to execute /usr/sbin/ip and read the host network namespace.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR snmpd.conf (5),
.BR snmpd (8),
.BR ip-link (8)
.PP
RFC 2741, Agent Extensibility (AgentX) Protocol Version 1.
.br
RFC 2863, The Interfaces Group MIB.
